  {
   "id": 17,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    -1620,
    -220
   ],
   "size": [
    720,
    200
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 0,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## qwen-edit-gguf.json\n\nInstruction edit + consistency\n\nU2 - Qwen-Image-Edit-2511 as GGUF Q4_K_M (Apache 2.0). THE fp8 build (19.6 GB + 7.9 GB encoder) hard-freezes this box; the Q4 quant (12.34 GB) FITS and completed in 380 s with cgroup peak 20.0 GB - 467 soft-limit throttles, but 0 hard-limit hits and 0 OOM kills (the memory guard in comfyui.service did its job). VAEEncode feeds the sampler latent AND both text encoders; FluxKontextMultiReferenceLatentMethod 'index_timestep_zero' is required for the Comfy repackaged files. 40 steps / cfg 3 is the non-Lightning recipe - add lightx2v's 4-step Lightning LoRA to make it fast. VERDICT vs Flux Kontext (E13): Qwen is far more FAITHFUL (preserves cottage, knight, framing) where Kontext re-dramatises and shifts composition - but 5.5x slower. Use Qwen when fidelity matters, Kontext when you want a bolder reinterpretation.\n\n---\n*How to run it: story **S5, S7** in `HOWTO.md`  ·  Why it is this way: **U2/E14c** in the scenarios' `EXPERIMENTS` logs.*"
   ],
   "color": "#332922",
   "bgcolor": "#593930"
  }
